$BTC  been on a solid rebound grind over the past 24 hours, flipping the script on that recent dip like it's no big deal. Price is cruising around $93,800 right now, up about 2.1% from yesterday $91,800 lows trading volume roaring at $77B+, up 15% as whales pile back in.

The fuel? Trump's signaling he's primed to ink that Bitcoin-friendly crypto bill, plus fresh ETF inflows hitting BlackRock's IBIT as OG holders cash out (but new bids incoming). Miners' costs are climbing to $74K/BTC, squeezing supply further, while on-chain fees spiked $353K. Market cap's a beast at $1.87T. Holding $92K support? Santa rally to $100K feels locked. King energy?

